  "extrapolation_note": "The early transient makes the all-point fit degenerate. On the bent second half the power-law floor is 2.562 (>= threshold, no crossing) and the exponential floor is 2.988; the last-8 power-law floor is 2.342 with a crossing at 94,047 steps (232 h). Only the floor-less log-linear form projects inside the budget (6.2-7.2 h), and it is the least physically appropriate model because it lets NLL fall without bound.",
  "decision": {
    "predeclared_rule": "Full R1 is justified only if the primary power-law-with-floor fit projects the threshold 2.3656425541851505 within <=12 h at the measured fastest clean rate; a floor at/above the threshold or a projection beyond the budget means a vehicle change.",
    "in_run_result": "The bounded run did not reach the threshold: held-out response-masked NLL 3.232435 at 6,592,512 sampled targets (step 1073, 7.99% of one epoch), 0.7668 nats above count.",
    "outcome": "NOT JUSTIFIED. Every identified floor model saturates at or above the threshold (2.34-3.0, bracketing the count itself); the optimistic crossing is 232 h and the realistic estimate is unreachable. The vehicle does not reach the R1 margin within a feasible budget.",
    "recommendation": "Change the R1 vehicle. The floor clustering at ~2.4-3.0 shows the blocker is not only exposure: at width 576 the graph converges toward the count level, not 0.10 nats below it. Address both the sequential op-count bottleneck (84.6% of step time, one busy core) and capacity. Ranked options with projections in the result document."
